        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Horticulture - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HORTICULTURE\n  +----------------------------------+\n  | Fruits, vegetables, flowers,     |\n  | ornamentals, nursery stock       |\n  | Intensive, high-value per acre   |\n  | High labor/acre, skilled work    |\n  | Many species per operation       |\n  | Perishable (hours to weeks)      |\n  | Price-maker (direct market)      |\n  +----------------------------------+\n                        |\n                        v\n               SHARED BIOLOGY:\n               Both are applied plant science.\n               Photosynthesis, transpiration, nutrient cycling,\n               soil microbiology — same mechanisms.\n               Horticulture applies them at finer precision,\n               higher inputs, higher outputs per area.\n```"
    },
