        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Horticulture - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nHORTICULTURE\n├── POMOLOGY (fruit science)\n│   Apples, pears, stone fruits, citrus, tropical fruits\n│   Focus: rootstock/scion relationships, training systems,\n│          harvest timing, post-harvest physiology\n│\n├── OLERICULTURE (vegetable production)\n│   Annuals and perennials grown for edible parts\n│   Focus: succession planting, season extension, crop scheduling,\n│          disease pressure management\n│\n├── FLORICULTURE (flower and ornamental plants)\n│   Cut flowers, potted plants, bedding plants\n│   Focus: floral quality, longevity, photoperiod control,\n│          color break management (virus), global supply chains\n│\n├── LANDSCAPE HORTICULTURE / ORNAMENTAL\n│   Woody ornamentals (trees, shrubs), groundcovers, perennials\n│   Focus: urban heat island, stormwater management,\n│          maintenance scheduling, IPM at civic scale\n│\n├── TURFGRASS SCIENCE\n│   Athletic fields, golf courses, home lawns\n│   Focus: wear tolerance, disease management, water use,\n│          aesthetic uniformity under stress\n│\n└── ARBORICULTURE (tree care)\n    Individual tree management in urban and parkland settings\n    Focus: structural assessment, pruning for safety and health,\n           soil management, root zone protection\n```"
    }
